# .clinerules-code

## Coding Standards for CliniRule Chrome Extension (Manifest V3)

This file outlines the coding standards and best practices that should be followed when contributing to the CliniRule Chrome extension using Manifest Version 3.

### Manifest V3 Compliance

- Ensure that the extension's manifest.json file follows the Manifest V3 specification.
- Use the appropriate API permissions and avoid unnecessary permissions.
- Implement declarative net request rules instead of blocking webRequest.

### Naming Conventions

- Use camelCase for variable and function names.
- Use PascalCase for class and component names.
- Use all-lowercase with underscores for constants.
- Prefix background script and content script file names with "background-" and "content-", respectively.

